            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for a judge, then the Malayalam for the accused."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: വിധി",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വിധി — vidhi — \"a verdict; fate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കോടതിയുടെ വിധി ഇന്ന് വരും. kōṭatiyuṭe vidhi innŭ varuṁ. The court's verdict will come today."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also fate, destiny: അത് എന്റെ വിധി (vidhi) ആയിരുന്നു, that was my fate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വിധി (vidhi) is borrowed from Sanskrit vidhi, \"rule\", and later \"fate\" (CDIAL 11755). A verdict is the rule a court lays down for one case."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
